##
#
# The Mach 10 double Mach reflection benchmark [2], Section 5.9
# (supplementary material), Figure 2 of [1].
#
# A Mach 10 shock impinges on a wall at an angle of 60 degrees. The
# computational domain is [0, 3.2] x [0, 1] with gamma = 1.4. Ahead of the
# shock the gas is at rest with rho = 1.4 and p = 1; the post-shock state
# is given by the Rankine-Hugoniot conditions (rho = 8, p = 116.5, v = 8.25
# (cos 30°, -sin 30°)). Slip boundary conditions are enforced on the wall
# {x >= 1/6, y = 0}, "do nothing" conditions on the outflow boundary
# {x = 3.2}, and the exact (moving shock) solution on all other boundaries.
#
# The chosen refinement level 6 corresponds to around 469k gridpoints,
# closest to the uniform Q1 mesh with 513600 nodes used in Figure 2 of [1],
# which shows a Schlieren plot of the density at t = 0.2. Refinement level
# 7 (the former benchmark configuration) corresponds to around 1.87M
# gridpoints (7.48M degrees of freedom).
#
# Note: The Q1 results of [1] were computed with "Code 3", a deal.II based
# precursor of ryujin that uses a smoothness-based high-order graph
# viscosity (psi(alpha) = alpha^4) instead of the entropy-viscosity
# commutator of ryujin, and the SSP(3,3) Runge-Kutta scheme (ssprk 33).
# This is a reconstruction, differences to the published figure are
# expected.
#
# The final time is set to t = 0.20 and we output a vtk every δt = 0.01.
# For postprocessing the simulation into a nice video set the output
# frequency to δt = 0.0005 which will result in a 20 seconds long video at
# 20 fps.
#
# [1] J.-L. Guermond, M. Nazarov, B. Popov, I. Tomas. Second-order invariant
#     domain preserving approximation of the Euler equations using convex
#     limiting. SIAM J. Sci. Comput., 40(5):A3211-A3239, 2018.
#     DOI 10.1137/17M1149961
#
# [2] P. Woodward, P. Colella. The numerical simulation of two-dimensional
#     fluid flow with strong shocks. J. Comput. Phys., 54(1):115-173, 1984.
#     DOI 10.1016/0021-9991(84)90142-6
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = mach10-dbmr

  set tasks             = vtu output

  set final time        = 0.20
  set timer granularity = 0.01
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 2
  set equation  = euler
  set gamma     = 1.4
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry            = wall

  set mesh refinement     = 6

  subsection wall
    set height        = 1
    set length        = 3.2
    set wall position = 0.166667
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = shock front

  set direction     = 0.8660254, -0.5
  set position      = 0.166667, 0

  subsection shock front
    set mach number     = 10
    set primitive state = 1.4, 0, 1
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.90
  set cfl max               = 0.90
  set cfl recovery strategy = none

  set time stepping scheme  = ssprk 33
end


subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection full
    set use mpi io     = true
    set schlieren beta = 10
  end
end
